{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>And he took the book of the covenant.</b> There is no earlier and later in the Torah — they are the admonitions, as stated in the Mekhilta. Rabbi Yishmael says: at the beginning of the matter, what does it say? 'And the land shall rest,' etc. — sabbatical years and jubilees, blessings and curses; and at the end of the matter, what does it say? 'These are the statutes and the judgments and the teachings.' They said: 'We accept upon ourselves.' Once he saw that they accepted upon themselves, he took the blood and sprinkled it on the people, as it says: 'And Moses took the blood and sprinkled it on the people.' He said to them: You are now held fast, bound, and tied; tomorrow come and accept upon yourselves all the commandments. 'We will do and we will hear' — we will do what is written here, and further <b>we will hear</b> if He wishes to command more."], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:00:12.724765225Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}